        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/23/apple-exploring-fix-for-safaris-cramped-layout-on-the-iphone-duos-outer-display/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2027/10/safari.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a new post on the WebKit blog highlighting what’s new in Safari 27.1, Apple’s Jen Simmons said the company is exploring ways to let websites make better use of the iPhone Duo’s outer display. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"iphone-duo\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1075581\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/23/apple-exploring-fix-for-safaris-cramped-layout-on-the-iphone-duos-outer-display/#more-1075581\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
