        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/23/ios-27-1-is-exclusive-to-iphone-duo-heres-why/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/ios-27.1-01.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">iOS 27.1 has officially launched, but you wouldn’t know it by checking your iPhone’s Settings app. That’s because the latest iPhone update is exclusive to iPhone Duo.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"ios-27,ios-27-1,iphone-duo\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1075476\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/23/ios-27-1-is-exclusive-to-iphone-duo-heres-why/#more-1075476\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
