        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/09/iphone-duo-front-display-hand.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">iPhone Duo launches this Friday (<a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/21/iphone-duo-review/\">read our full review here</a>), but there’s one software feature Apple says won’t be ready until later this year: Reachability.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"iphone,iphone-duo\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1075181\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/10/21/iphone-duo-will-add-reachability-feature-later-this-year/#more-1075181\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
